# =====================================================================
#  dyadseed.la — 0 and 1 beneath the nine primitives.
#
#  ── THE QUESTION THIS ANSWERS ───────────────────────────────────────
#  Erik: "What about the dyad? What about the power of 2, if at all?" — and,
#  more sharply, that 1 and 0 should START the glyphic sequence.
#
#  `archroot.la` finds that only THREE of the nine primitives derive from the
#  root (SELF, RECOGNITION, LOVE) and SIX are UNDERIVED — THE GAP, per Erik's
#  ruling 2026-08-24, and NOT a settled result; none is forced into a
#  derivation. (`archderive.la` then ATTEMPTS the six: BEING resolves as the
#  root itself, the other five are AXIOMS with the seam stated.) Taken as a
#  derivation
#  chain, "0 and 1 generate the nine" contradicts that finding directly.
#
#  ★★ BUT 0 AND 1 ARE ALREADY AT THE BASE OF THE NINE, AND THIS MODULE
#  WITNESSES IT BY REDUCTION RATHER THAN BY ASSERTION:
#
#        VOID     = la a. la b. b                   IS Church ZERO
#        BEING    = la self. self                   IS Church ONE
#        BECOMING = la n. la f. la x. f(n(f)(x))    IS the SUCCESSOR
#
#  BEING being ONE is not a coincidence and not a pun: the identity function is
#  eta-equivalent to la f. la x. f(x). Probed, VAL(BEING) = VAL(ONE) = "|".
#  So Erik's "1 and 0 start the glyphic sequence" is CORRECT, and the two are
#  the primitives already in the catalogue -- VOID and BEING.
#
#  So the naturals are generated beneath TWO of the nine, and `cob.la`'s first
#  cosmogenic beat is literally ⊗(VOID, BEING) — "the first distinction arises
#  from the undifferentiated", the 0/1 dyad enacted.
#
#  ── THE DISTINCTION THAT KEEPS BOTH TRUE ────────────────────────────
#  0 and 1 GROUND THE ARITHMETIC STRATUM. They do NOT generate the nine.
#  That is the same shape as the five vowel nuclei sitting beneath the nine
#  phonyms: a layer underneath, not a derivation above. Stated this way the
#  dyad seed and archroot's six UNDERIVED primitives are compatible; stated as a
#  derivation chain they are not, and archroot's reduction gates would rightly
#  go RED. This module asserts ONLY the reduction facts.
#
#  ── AND THE POWERS OF 2, HONESTLY ───────────────────────────────────
#  Self-combining a glyph grows the stored DAG LINEARLY (1,2,3,4,5,6) while the
#  unfolded tree grows as 2^(n+1)−1 (1,3,7,15,31,63). That exponent is real and
#  measured — and it is EXACTLY AND ONLY binary branching, the counting shadow
#  of arity-2. Nothing produces powers of two by any other mechanism.
#  ★ The deeper reading is better than a numerological one: 2^n is the cost the
#  language REFUSES TO PAY. The seal keeps one glyph while the tree it means
#  doubles. The power of two is present as the thing defeated, not as a
#  signature.
# =====================================================================

glyph IF   = la c. la t. la f. c(t)(f)("!")
glyph AND  = la p. la q. p(q)(p)
glyph NOT  = la p. la t. la f. p(f)(t)

# ── the two primitives under test, verbatim from primitives_spec.la ──
glyph VOID     = la a. la b. b
glyph BECOMING = la n. la f. la x. f(n(f)(x))
glyph BEING    = la self. self

# ── a Church numeral is probed by what it DOES, not by what it is called ──
# n(MARK)("") builds a string of n marks, so the numeral's value is readable.
glyph MARK  = la s. concat("|")(s)
glyph VAL   = la n. n(MARK)("")

# ── 1. VOID IS ZERO — not "like" zero, reducible to it ──────────────
# Church zero is la f. la x. x, which is la a. la b. b up to the names of its
# binders. The probe: applied to any successor-step and any seed, it yields the
# seed untouched — no application ever happens.
glyph ZERO_OK = str_eq(VAL(VOID))("")

# ── 2. BECOMING IS THE SUCCESSOR ────────────────────────────────────
glyph ONE   = BECOMING(VOID)
glyph TWO   = BECOMING(ONE)
glyph THREE = BECOMING(TWO)
glyph SUCC_OK = AND(str_eq(VAL(ONE))("|"))
                   (AND(str_eq(VAL(TWO))("||"))(str_eq(VAL(THREE))("|||")))

# ── 3. ★ THE ARITHMETIC STRATUM IS GENERATED, AND ONLY IT ───────────
# Iterating the successor from VOID reaches every natural. That is the whole
# claim: a stratum beneath the primitives, not a derivation of them.
glyph Z    = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph ITER = Z(la self. la k. IF(int_eq(k)(0))(la _. VOID)(la _. BECOMING(self(sub(k)(1)))))
glyph REP  = Z(la self. la k. IF(int_eq(k)(0))(la _. "")(la _. concat("|")(self(sub(k)(1)))))
glyph STRATUM_OK = AND(str_eq(VAL(ITER(5)))(REP(5)))(str_eq(VAL(ITER(9)))(REP(9)))

# ── 4. ★ BEING IS ONE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
glyph BEING_IS_ONE = str_eq(VAL(BEING))(VAL(ONE))

# ── 5. ★★ AND THE BOUND, PROVED RATHER THAN ASSERTED ────────────────
# Does the seed GENERATE the nine? No -- and the reason is exact: the map down
# to numerals is NOT INJECTIVE, so it cannot be inverted. SELF = BEING(BEING)
# is the identity applied to itself, hence the identity again, hence ONE. So
# BEING and SELF -- two DISTINCT glyphs, which canon keeps distinct (SELF is
# the normal form of the rewrite ↻(BEING)) -- collapse to the SAME numeral.
# A projection that loses a distinction cannot generate what it lost.
#
# So both things are true at once, which is what the ruling needs:
#   0 and 1 GROUND the arithmetic stratum beneath the primitives -- witnessed.
#   0 and 1 do NOT DERIVE the nine -- archroot's six remain UNDERIVED (THE GAP,
#   per Erik's ruling 2026-08-24). ⚠️ This module may NOT be cited as that chain.
# Claimed as a derivation chain it is false; claimed as a stratum it is proved.
glyph SELF_ = BEING(BEING)
glyph SEED_BOUND = AND(str_eq(VAL(SELF_))(VAL(BEING)))
                      (NOT(str_eq(VAL(SELF_))(VAL(VOID))))

glyph MK = la c. IF(c)(la _. "OK")(la _. "FAIL")
glyph MAIN = print(
  concat(concat(concat("dyadseed VOID=0 ")(MK(ZERO_OK)))
                (concat(" | BECOMING=succ ")(MK(SUCC_OK))))
        (concat(concat(" | stratum ")(MK(STRATUM_OK)))
               (concat(concat(" | BEING=1 ")(MK(BEING_IS_ONE)))(concat(" | bound(projection not injective) ")(MK(SEED_BOUND))))))

export VOID BECOMING VAL ITER
